/*
:name: signed_cast_derived_width
:type: error
:tolg: 1
:error: `Signed\(...\)` reinterpret needs a fully-typed input
:help: give the operand a sized type
*/
// `Signed(x)` keeps x's bit width and re-reads its top bit as the sign, so x
// must have a DECLARED width (a typed name, a bit-select). An arithmetic
// result only has the range the bitwidth analysis derived, and that depends
// on how tight the analysis is: `a / 17 * 17` derives [0, 255] (8 bits, so 255
// reads as -1) while the identical `a - a % 17` derives [-16, 255] (9 bits,
// 255 stays 255). Both used to compile to different values.
pub mod signed_cast_derived_width(a:U8) -> (y1:S16@[0]) {
  y1 = Signed(a / 17 * 17)   // locate_error_here
}
